# Author   : Sylvain Deguire (VA2OPS)
# Date     : 3 November 2026
# Purpose  : udev rule for the Kenwood IF-232C CAT interface over USB.
#            Field-validated with Pierre VE2EH's Kenwood TS-850
#            (CAT = IF-232C, audio = SignaLink; see 84-et-signalink.rules).
#
# The IF-232C is a TTL<->RS-232 level converter for the radio's ACC port. On a
# modern PC it is reached through a USB-serial cable; Pierre's is a Prolific
# PL2303 variant (067b:23a3, "ATEN Serial Bridge"). Tag it as ET_CAT and start
# rigctld — the active radio profile (e.g. TS-850: Hamlib model 2009, 4800 baud,
# PTT=RIG) drives everything else via wrapper-rigctld.sh.
#
# The ENV{ET_DEVICE}=="" guard claims it only if no earlier, more specific rule
# already matched. NOTE the comma before RUN+= — rigctld will not start without
# it (same gotcha fixed earlier in the DigiRig Lite rule).
#
# Postconditions:
# 1. /dev/et-cat created
# 2. rigctld is started

SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="067b", ATTRS{idProduct}=="23a3", ENV{ET_DEVICE}=="", \
    ACTION=="add", \
    ENV{ET_DEVICE}="IF-232C", ENV{ET_SUBDEVICE}="CAT", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660", SYMLINK+="et-cat", \
    RUN+="/usr/bin/systemctl start rigctld"
